Fix misaligned __boot_sync causing store-misaligned trap (mcause=6) at boot.

Upstream bug in ucb-bar/libgloss-htif @ 39234a16: __boot_sync (.word, written
by sw in BARRIER_PASS) is declared in .bss without an alignment directive, so
crtmain.o's .bss has alignment 1. With the Ubuntu apt picolibc toolchain, the
1-byte __lock___libc_recursive_mutex lands immediately before it and
__boot_sync ends up at an odd address -> sw traps -> handle_trap -> _exit(6).
Latent with newlib (conda flow) only by link-order luck; would also trap on
real Rocket cores, not just spike.

Apply: git -C /work/chipyard/toolchains/libgloss apply <this file>
Diagnosed: phases/P0-environment/actual.md 2026-06-11, log results/raw/p0-step3e-libgloss.log

diff --git a/misc/crtmain-argv.S b/misc/crtmain-argv.S
index 169f240..e93d9d8 100644
--- a/misc/crtmain-argv.S
+++ b/misc/crtmain-argv.S
@@ -55,5 +55,6 @@ argv:
     .dc.a 0
 argc:
     .word 0
+    .balign 4
 __boot_sync:
     .word 0
diff --git a/misc/crtmain.S b/misc/crtmain.S
index 457ffb6..e358290 100644
--- a/misc/crtmain.S
+++ b/misc/crtmain.S
@@ -34,5 +34,6 @@ name:
     .asciz "chipyard"

     .bss
+    .balign 4
 __boot_sync:
     .word 0
